th"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong for the sole managed node: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, reboot was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and the worker, UID, configuration checksums, networking, SSH, and node agent recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe is systemd-specific and unsupported on Alpine, so it cannot independently inventory failed OpenRC services; direct executor observations nevertheless show the worker and core services started.","The final lifecycle inventory covers /tmp but not /var/tmp, so final persistence of /var/tmp/inventory-worker-reboot.log is not directly observed.","The topology and task provide no separate application dataset or multi-node cluster state; restart recovery evidence therefore consists of persistent service/configuration checksums plus healthy node services."]}
